From 3a04468271ee976cde5c02324513aa5bb2fd7b8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: changeforan <7800290+changeforan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 19:20:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] wined3d: Implement HEVC Main decoding over Vulkan Video.

Translate DXVA_PicParams_HEVC into the StdVideoH265 video, sequence and
picture parameter sets, and submit slices through vkCmdDecodeVideoKHR.

Note that DXVA's RefPicSetStCurrBefore/After/LtCurr arrays hold indices
into RefPicList, whereas Vulkan expects DPB slot indices, so they are
remapped while walking the reference list.

The quantisation matrix buffer is sized per codec: DXVA_Qmatrix_HEVC is
1000 bytes against 224 for H.264, as HEVC adds the 16x16 and 32x32
scaling lists.
